Looking at the comment: "After removal, none of the elements remaining in the priority queue are contained in c."

I need to express that for every element remaining in the queue (indices 0 to size-1), that element is not contained in c.

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); !c.contains(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the comment: "After removal, none of the elements remaining in the priority queue are contained in c."

This means for every element currently in the queue (after the operation), `c` does not contain it. I use `get(i)` and `size()` as observers, ranging over all valid indices.

